IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccwa-jurisdiction`

-- Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the
-- situation as parameters, so that one deployment serves every seat and the question form drops the questions that do
-- not arise.
--
-- SEATS (`my role`, the first input of every exported question, "Which of these describes you"):
--   * the child charged, or the person who was a child at the offence -- the baseline's seat, whose 20 questions are
--     asked here by calling the baseline's functions in ccwa-jurisdiction.l4;
--   * a parent or guardian of the child -- whom the Court may order to attend, on a $500 penalty, in proceedings that are
--     not for an offence (s 23), who may be excluded from the courtroom (s 31), and who is bound by s 36;
--   * the victim, or someone else affected by the offence -- who may be given the child's name, age, address and the
--     charge after a closed hearing (s 31(2)), and who is bound by s 36;
--   * a publisher or broadcaster, or anyone who would pass on what happened -- bound by ss 35 and 36, on a fine of
--     $10 000 or 12 months' imprisonment.
-- A question about another role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input. The Court, the
-- President, a magistrate, a prescribed officer, the Attorney General and the Commissioner of Police are never seats:
-- what they may or must do appears as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the graffiti encoding): within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that
-- situation's fact straight after `my role`, and when it does not hold answers `does not arise for you` without reading
-- anything else. There is one situation input, shared by every role, so the form asks it once:
--   * `how the case in the Children's Court has ended` (an enumeration: `it has not ended yet`, `the charge was
--     dismissed`, `the child was found guilty or convicted, and an order was made`). The child's three questions about an
--     order made against them (ss 28, 34(3), 40) arise only for the last value; the four questions of s 36 (each role's
--     question about telling others how the case ended) arise for the last two.
-- Every other question arises in every situation of its role and takes no situation input. The two helpers that read
-- the situation list every value, with no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
--
-- No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input. The baseline's `My charge` record is taken as the baseline takes
-- it.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened`
    `I am a parent or guardian of the child`
    `I am the victim of the offence, or someone else affected by it`
    `I publish or broadcast reports, or would pass on what happened in the case`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Penalty` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `fine or imprisonment` HAS `the fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
                               `the imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Court answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `court` HAS `which` IS A `Court for my charge`

DECLARE `Custody answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `cap` HAS `the cap` IS A `Custody cap`

-- The one situation (D8), shared by every role.
DECLARE `How the case has ended` IS ONE OF
    `it has not ended yet`
    `the charge was dismissed`
    `the child was found guilty or convicted, and an order was made`

-- s 36(1)'s exceptions, from the side of a person other than the child.
DECLARE `Who I would tell` IS ONE OF
    `a court`
    `someone performing duties under a written law`
    `someone whose duties concern the child's custody or welfare`
    `a health department officer, for the Developmental Pathways Project`
    `an employer, a neighbour or anyone else`

§§ `Carrying the baseline's answers, and the helpers the new seats need`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- s 23(2): "Penalty: $500."
`the most a parent can be fined for not attending` MEANS 500

-- ss 35(4)(b), 36(2)(b): "after summary conviction by a fine of $10 000 or imprisonment for 12 months". The fine is the
-- baseline's; the 12 months are read from the deposited text.
`the imprisonment for identifying a child, in months` MEANS 12

GIVETH A `Penalty`
`the penalty for identifying a child` MEANS
    `fine or imprisonment` (`What fine can someone who identifies me be given`) `the imprisonment for identifying a child, in months`

-- The situation. Every value is listed, with no OTHERWISE.
GIVEN `how` IS A `How the case has ended`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the case has ended, as told` IF
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `it has not ended yet` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the charge was dismissed` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the child was found guilty or convicted, and an order was made` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `how` IS A `How the case has ended`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an order has been made, as told` IF
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `it has not ended yet` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the charge was dismissed` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the child was found guilty or convicted, and an order was made` THEN TRUE

-- The person told, as the baseline's `Recipient`, value for value.
GIVEN `who` IS A `Who I would tell`
GIVETH A `Recipient`
`the recipient, as the child puts it` `who` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `a court` THEN `a court of law`
    WHEN `someone performing duties under a written law` THEN `a person performing duties under a written law`
    WHEN `someone whose duties concern the child's custody or welfare` THEN `a person whose duties concern my custody or welfare`
    WHEN `a health department officer, for the Developmental Pathways Project` THEN `a health department officer for the Developmental Pathways Project`
    WHEN `an employer, a neighbour or anyone else` THEN `an employer or anyone else`

§§ `For the child before the court (the baseline's seat)`

-- Each question calls the baseline's function of the same subject (ccwa-jurisdiction.l4) and restates no rule: for
-- this role, and where its situation holds, its answer is the baseline's, carried in the answer types above.

§§§ `ss 3, 19 -- am I a child for this charge`

@export Am I a child for the purposes of this charge in the Children's Court (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) ss 3, 19)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the date of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The date the offence was (or is said to have been) committed
      `my age is uncertain and the charge says I might have been a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your age at the time is uncertain and the charge alleges you might have been under 18
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I a child for the purposes of my charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN `yes if` (`Am I a child for this charge` `my date of birth` `the date of the offence` `my age is uncertain and the charge says I might have been a child`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 19B -- may I choose a trial on indictment`

@export May I choose to be tried on indictment by the Supreme Court or District Court (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 19B(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the charge` IS A `My charge` @desc The charge against you and what the Court has decided about it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I choose to be tried on indictment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN `yes if` (`May I elect to be tried on indictment` `the charge`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the Children's Court tell me that I may choose a trial on indictment (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 19B(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the charge` IS A `My charge` @desc The charge against you and what the Court has decided about it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the Court tell me that I may choose a trial on indictment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN `yes if` (`Must the Court tell me I may elect a trial on indictment` `the charge`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I have a jury if I stay in the Children's Court for an indictable charge (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 19B(4)(c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I have a jury if I stay in the Children's Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN `yes if` (`Can I have a jury in the Children's Court`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 19, 19B-19D, 30 -- which court deals with my charge`

@export Which court deals with my charge (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) ss 19, 19B, 19C, 19D, 30)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the charge` IS A `My charge` @desc The charge against you and what the Court has decided about it
GIVETH A `Court answer`
`Which court deals with my charge, for me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN `court` (`Which court deals with my charge` `the charge`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Could the Children's Court send my charge to the Magistrates Court because I have turned 18 (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 19D)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the charge` IS A `My charge` @desc The charge against you and what the Court has decided about it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Could my charge be sent to the Magistrates Court because I have turned 18` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN `yes if` (`Could my charge be transferred because I have turned 18` `the charge`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I choose to pay a prescribed penalty instead of being prosecuted (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 19(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `another written law offers that choice for this simple offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another law lets a person pay a set penalty instead of being prosecuted for this simple offence
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I choose to pay a prescribed penalty instead of being prosecuted` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN `yes if` (`May I elect to pay a prescribed penalty instead` `another written law offers that choice for this simple offence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 21, 22 -- how much the Court as constituted can give me`

@export What is the most detention or imprisonment the Children's Court, as constituted, can give me (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) ss 21, 22)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `who sits` IS A `Who sits` @desc Who constitutes the Court at your sentencing
      `the kind` IS A `Kind of custody` @desc Detention or imprisonment
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the date of sentencing` IS A DATE @desc The day you are sentenced
GIVETH A `Custody answer`
`What is the most detention or imprisonment the Court as constituted can give me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN `cap` (`What is the most custody the Court can give me` `who sits` `the kind` `my date of birth` `the date of sentencing`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the magistrate tell me at the start that they have a judge's sentencing powers (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 22(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the President directed the magistrate under s 22` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the President gave the magistrate extended powers for your charge
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the magistrate tell me at the start of extended sentencing powers` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN `yes if` (`Must the magistrate tell me of extended powers` `the President directed the magistrate under s 22`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 23 -- must my parent or guardian be made to come`

@export Must the Children's Court order my parent or guardian to attend, under this Act (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 23)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `these are proceedings against me for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are charged with an offence (then the Young Offenders Act 1994 s 45 applies instead)
      `a parent or guardian is present` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a parent or guardian of yours is in court
      `the Court finds a valid reason to excuse attendance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court considers there is a valid reason to excuse a parent's attendance
      `the Court finds it unreasonable to delay for a parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court considers it not reasonable to delay for a parent or guardian
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the Court order my parent or guardian to attend, under this Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN `yes if` (`Must the Court order my parent or guardian to attend under this Act` `these are proceedings against me for an offence` `a parent or guardian is present` `the Court finds a valid reason to excuse attendance` `the Court finds it unreasonable to delay for a parent`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 31, 33, 34 -- who may be present, and what I must understand`

@export May this person stay in the courtroom at my hearing (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) ss 31, 33)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person` IS A `Person in the courtroom` @desc Who wants to be in the courtroom
      `the Court ordered this person excluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has ordered under s 31 that this person (or persons including them) leave
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May this person stay in the courtroom at my hearing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN `yes if` (`May this person stay in the courtroom` `the person` `the Court ordered this person excluded`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the Court give this person my name, age, address and the charge after a closed hearing (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 31(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Court made an exclusion order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court excluded people from the hearing under s 31(1)
      `the hearing has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the hearing is over
      `the person satisfied the Court of loss from the offence or other good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person showed the Court they lost something because of the offence, or had other good cause
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the Court give this person my name, age, address and the charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN `yes if` (`Must the Court give this person my name and address` `the Court made an exclusion order` `the hearing has concluded` `the person satisfied the Court of loss from the offence or other good cause`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the Children's Court make sure I understand what the proceedings are about (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 34(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the Court make sure I understand what the proceedings are about` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN `yes if` (`Must the Court make sure I understand the proceedings`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the order against me saved, though the Court's explanation fell short (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 34(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how the case in the Children's Court has ended` IS A `How the case has ended` @desc How the case in the Children's Court has ended, if it has: not yet; the charge was dismissed; or the child was found guilty or convicted, and an order was made (the questions on what follows arise only once it has ended)
      `the Court substantially complied with s 34` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court substantially did what s 34 requires
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the order against me saved though the explanation fell short` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN
        IF `an order has been made, as told` `how the case in the Children's Court has ended`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my order saved despite a short explanation` `the Court substantially complied with s 34`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 35, 36A -- may I be identified in a report`

@export May a report that identifies me as the accused be published (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) ss 35, 36A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where` IS A `Where I am tried` @desc The court whose proceedings the report is about
      `the Supreme Court allowed it under s 36A or the PBO Act s 34 permits it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Supreme Court order under s 36A (or the Prohibited Behaviour Orders Act 2010 s 34) allows it
      `that court ordered no publication under s 35(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the Supreme or District Court, whether it ordered that the child not be identified
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May a report that identifies me be published` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN `yes if` (`May a report identifying me be published` `where` `the Supreme Court allowed it under s 36A or the PBO Act s 34 permits it` `that court ordered no publication under s 35(2)`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What fine can someone who unlawfully identifies me be given on summary conviction, in dollars (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) ss 35(4), 36(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What fine can someone who unlawfully identifies me be given` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN `amount` (`What fine can someone who identifies me be given`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May this person ask the Supreme Court to allow my identification (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 36A(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the applicant` IS AN `Applicant` @desc Who wants to apply
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May this person ask the Supreme Court to allow my identification` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN `yes if` (`May this person apply to allow my identification` `the applicant`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 36, 36AA -- may someone tell others how my case ended`

-- Asked only once the case has ended in a dismissal or a finding of guilt, so the baseline's second fact is TRUE by
-- the situation's own terms.
@export May someone other than me tell this person, in a way that identifies me, how my Children's Court case ended (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) ss 36, 36AA)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how the case in the Children's Court has ended` IS A `How the case has ended` @desc How the case in the Children's Court has ended, if it has: not yet; the charge was dismissed; or the child was found guilty or convicted, and an order was made (the questions on what follows arise only once it has ended)
      `the recipient` IS A `Recipient` @desc Who would be told
      `a Supreme Court order under s 36A or the PBO Act s 34 allows it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Supreme Court order under s 36A (or the Prohibited Behaviour Orders Act 2010 s 34) allows it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May someone other than me tell this person how my case ended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN
        IF `the case has ended, as told` `how the case in the Children's Court has ended`
        THEN `yes if` (`May someone else disclose how my case ended` `the recipient` TRUE `a Supreme Court order under s 36A or the PBO Act s 34 allows it`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 28, 40 -- can I have it looked at again`

@export Can I ask the President of the Children's Court to reconsider the order made against me (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 40)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how the case in the Children's Court has ended` IS A `How the case has ended` @desc How the case in the Children's Court has ended, if it has: not yet; the charge was dismissed; or the child was found guilty or convicted, and an order was made (the questions on what follows arise only once it has ended)
      `a judge sat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court that made the order consisted of or included a judge
      `the date of the order` IS A DATE @desc The date the order was made
      `the date I apply` IS A DATE @desc The date you would apply
      `leave to appeal has been granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether leave to appeal against the same order has been granted under s 41
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I ask the President to reconsider the order made against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN
        IF `an order has been made, as told` `how the case in the Children's Court has ended`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I ask the President to reconsider my order` `a judge sat` `the date of the order` `the date I apply` `leave to appeal has been granted`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I apply for my case to be reheard (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 28)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how the case in the Children's Court has ended` IS A `How the case has ended` @desc How the case in the Children's Court has ended, if it has: not yet; the charge was dismissed; or the child was found guilty or convicted, and an order was made (the questions on what follows arise only once it has ended)
      `the order was made under the Young Offenders Act 1994 or the Children and Community Services Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order against you was made under one of those Acts
      `it followed a conviction on indictment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order followed a conviction on indictment
      `the proceedings are themselves a rehearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proceedings were already a rehearing under s 28
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I apply for my case to be reheard` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child charged, or I was a child when the offence is said to have happened` THEN
        IF `an order has been made, as told` `how the case in the Children's Court has ended`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I apply for a rehearing` `the order was made under the Young Offenders Act 1994 or the Children and Community Services Act 2004` `it followed a conviction on indictment` `the proceedings are themselves a rehearing`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a parent or guardian of the child (ss 23, 31, 34, 36)`

-- s 23 lets the Court order a parent or guardian to attend, on a $500 penalty, but not in proceedings for an offence,
-- which the Young Offenders Act 1994 s 45 governs (s 23(1a)); s 36 binds "a person other than the child", the parent
-- included.

§§§ `s 23 -- must I attend`

@export Must the Children's Court order me, as a parent or guardian, to attend all stages of the proceedings about my child (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 23(1), (1a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `these are proceedings against my child for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is charged with an offence (then the Young Offenders Act 1994 s 45 applies instead of s 23)
      `a parent or guardian of my child is present` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or another parent or guardian of the child is in court
      `the Court finds a valid reason to excuse attendance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court considers there is a valid reason to excuse a parent's attendance
      `the Court finds it unreasonable to delay for a parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court considers it not reasonable to delay for a parent or guardian
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the Court order me to attend my child's proceedings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent or guardian of the child` THEN `yes if` (`Must the Court order my parent or guardian to attend under this Act` `these are proceedings against my child for an offence` `a parent or guardian of my child is present` `the Court finds a valid reason to excuse attendance` `the Court finds it unreasonable to delay for a parent`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined if I fail, without reasonable excuse, to comply with an order to attend (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 23(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for not complying with an order to attend` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent or guardian of the child` THEN `amount` `the most a parent can be fined for not attending`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If the Court went on without any parent or guardian, must it do what it reasonably can to tell me in writing of the charge, its findings and orders (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 23(1a), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `these are proceedings against my child for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is charged with an offence (then the Young Offenders Act 1994 s 45 applies instead of s 23)
      `the Court went on without any parent or guardian present` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court heard and decided the proceedings with no parent or guardian of the child there (s 23(3))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the Court try to tell me in writing what happened if it went on without me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent or guardian of the child` THEN `yes if` ((NOT `these are proceedings against my child for an offence`) AND `the Court went on without any parent or guardian present`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 31, 34 -- in the courtroom`

@export May I stay in the courtroom at my child's hearing (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 31(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Court ordered me excluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has ordered under s 31(1) that you (or persons including you) leave the courtroom
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I stay in the courtroom at my child's hearing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent or guardian of the child` THEN `yes if` (`May this person stay in the courtroom` `my parent or guardian` `the Court ordered me excluded`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the Children's Court make sure my child understands what the proceedings are about (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 34(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the Court make sure my child understands the proceedings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent or guardian of the child` THEN `yes if` `Must the Court make sure I understand the proceedings`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 36 -- telling others how the case ended`

@export May I tell this person, in a way that identifies my child, how the Children's Court case ended (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) ss 36, 36AA)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how the case in the Children's Court has ended` IS A `How the case has ended` @desc How the case in the Children's Court has ended, if it has: not yet; the charge was dismissed; or the child was found guilty or convicted, and an order was made (the questions on what follows arise only once it has ended)
      `the person I would tell` IS A `Who I would tell` @desc Who would be told: a court; a person performing duties under a written law; a person whose duties concern the child's custody or welfare; a health department officer for the Developmental Pathways Project (s 36AA); or an employer, a neighbour or anyone else
      `a Supreme Court order under s 36A or the PBO Act s 34 allows it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Supreme Court order under s 36A (or the Prohibited Behaviour Orders Act 2010 s 34) allows it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I tell this person how my child's case ended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent or guardian of the child` THEN
        IF `the case has ended, as told` `how the case in the Children's Court has ended`
        THEN `yes if` (`May someone else disclose how my case ended` (`the recipient, as the child puts it` `the person I would tell`) TRUE `a Supreme Court order under s 36A or the PBO Act s 34 allows it`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined or imprisoned, on summary conviction, for disclosing how my child's case ended when s 36 forbids it (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 36(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Penalty`
`What is the most I can be given for telling others unlawfully how my child's case ended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent or guardian of the child` THEN `the penalty for identifying a child`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the victim, or someone else affected by the offence (ss 31, 33, 36, 36A)`

-- s 31(2) entitles a person who suffered loss by the offence, or has other good cause, to the child's name, age,
-- address and the charge after a closed hearing; ss 35 and 36 bind the victim as they bind anyone.

§§§ `ss 31, 33, 36A -- at the hearing, and after it`

@export May I stay in the courtroom at the child's hearing (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) ss 31(1), 33)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Court ordered me excluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has ordered under s 31(1) that you (or persons including you) leave the courtroom
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I stay in the courtroom at the hearing, as the victim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the victim of the offence, or someone else affected by it` THEN `yes if` (`May this person stay in the courtroom` `the victim` `the Court ordered me excluded`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export After a closed hearing, must the Court give me the child's name, age and address and the particulars of the charge (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 31(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Court made an exclusion order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court excluded people from the hearing under s 31(1)
      `the hearing has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the hearing is over
      `I satisfy the Court that the offence caused me loss, or that I have other good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you show the Court that you suffered loss because of the offence the child committed, or that you have other good cause
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the Court give me the child's name, age, address and the charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the victim of the offence, or someone else affected by it` THEN `yes if` (`Must the Court give this person my name and address` `the Court made an exclusion order` `the hearing has concluded` `I satisfy the Court that the offence caused me loss, or that I have other good cause`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I ask the Supreme Court to allow the child to be identified (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 36A(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I ask the Supreme Court to allow the child to be identified, as the victim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the victim of the offence, or someone else affected by it` THEN `yes if` (`May this person apply to allow my identification` `the victim`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 36, 36A -- telling others`

@export May I tell this person, in a way that identifies the child, how the Children's Court case ended (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) ss 36, 36AA)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how the case in the Children's Court has ended` IS A `How the case has ended` @desc How the case in the Children's Court has ended, if it has: not yet; the charge was dismissed; or the child was found guilty or convicted, and an order was made (the questions on what follows arise only once it has ended)
      `the person I would tell` IS A `Who I would tell` @desc Who would be told: a court; a person performing duties under a written law; a person whose duties concern the child's custody or welfare; a health department officer for the Developmental Pathways Project (s 36AA); or an employer, a neighbour or anyone else
      `a Supreme Court order under s 36A or the PBO Act s 34 allows it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Supreme Court order under s 36A (or the Prohibited Behaviour Orders Act 2010 s 34) allows it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I tell this person how the child's case ended, as the victim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the victim of the offence, or someone else affected by it` THEN
        IF `the case has ended, as told` `how the case in the Children's Court has ended`
        THEN `yes if` (`May someone else disclose how my case ended` (`the recipient, as the child puts it` `the person I would tell`) TRUE `a Supreme Court order under s 36A or the PBO Act s 34 allows it`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined or imprisoned, on summary conviction, for disclosing how the child's case ended when s 36 forbids it (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 36(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Penalty`
`What is the most I can be given for telling others unlawfully how the child's case ended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the victim of the offence, or someone else affected by it` THEN `the penalty for identifying a child`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a publisher, broadcaster or anyone who would pass on what happened (ss 31, 35, 36, 36A)`

-- s 35 binds whoever publishes or broadcasts a report likely to identify the child; s 36 whoever discloses how the
-- case ended. Only the Attorney General or the Commissioner of Police may ask the Supreme Court to allow it (s 36A(3)).

§§§ `ss 31, 35, 36A -- reporting the case`

@export May I publish or broadcast a report of the proceedings that is likely to identify the child as the accused (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) ss 35(1), (2), 36A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the court` IS A `Where I am tried` @desc The court whose proceedings the report is about: the Children's Court; a court hearing an appeal from it; or the Supreme Court or District Court, not on appeal from the Children's Court
      `the Supreme Court allowed it under s 36A or the PBO Act s 34 permits it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Supreme Court order under s 36A (or the Prohibited Behaviour Orders Act 2010 s 34) allows it
      `that court ordered no publication under s 35(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the Supreme or District Court, whether it ordered that the child not be identified
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I publish a report that identifies the child` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I publish or broadcast reports, or would pass on what happened in the case` THEN `yes if` (`May a report identifying me be published` `the court` `the Supreme Court allowed it under s 36A or the PBO Act s 34 permits it` `that court ordered no publication under s 35(2)`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined or imprisoned, on summary conviction, for publishing a report that identifies the child, or disclosing how the case ended, when the Act forbids it (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) ss 35(4), 36(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Penalty`
`What is the most I can be given for publishing or disclosing unlawfully` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I publish or broadcast reports, or would pass on what happened in the case` THEN `the penalty for identifying a child`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I stay in the courtroom at the child's hearing as a reporter (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 31(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Court ordered me excluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has ordered under s 31(1) that you (or persons including you) leave the courtroom
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I stay in the courtroom as a reporter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I publish or broadcast reports, or would pass on what happened in the case` THEN `yes if` (`May this person stay in the courtroom` `a reporter` `the Court ordered me excluded`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I, as a publisher or broadcaster, ask the Supreme Court to allow the child to be identified (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) s 36A(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I ask the Supreme Court to allow the child to be identified, as a publisher` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I publish or broadcast reports, or would pass on what happened in the case` THEN `yes if` (`May this person apply to allow my identification` `a newspaper or broadcaster`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 36 -- passing on how the case ended`

@export May I tell this person, in a way that identifies the child, how the Children's Court case ended (Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA) ss 36, 36AA)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how the case in the Children's Court has ended` IS A `How the case has ended` @desc How the case in the Children's Court has ended, if it has: not yet; the charge was dismissed; or the child was found guilty or convicted, and an order was made (the questions on what follows arise only once it has ended)
      `the person I would tell` IS A `Who I would tell` @desc Who would be told: a court; a person performing duties under a written law; a person whose duties concern the child's custody or welfare; a health department officer for the Developmental Pathways Project (s 36AA); or an employer, a neighbour or anyone else
      `a Supreme Court order under s 36A or the PBO Act s 34 allows it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Supreme Court order under s 36A (or the Prohibited Behaviour Orders Act 2010 s 34) allows it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I pass on how the child's case ended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I publish or broadcast reports, or would pass on what happened in the case` THEN
        IF `the case has ended, as told` `how the case in the Children's Court has ended`
        THEN `yes if` (`May someone else disclose how my case ended` (`the recipient, as the child puts it` `the person I would tell`) TRUE `a Supreme Court order under s 36A or the PBO Act s 34 allows it`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
